            "description": "Parse CSV with required headers id,name,email,first_choice,second_choice,group_id, preserving row order and these fields. Trim surrounding whitespace on every field, collapse internal whitespace in names, and lowercase emails. Preserve case of IDs and preferences. Reject malformed rows, missing IDs, duplicate IDs among previously accepted rows, empty names, invalid emails (require one @ with nonempty local and domain portions and no whitespace), unknown or empty first_choice, and nonempty second_choice not in workshop_ids. Empty second_choice is permitted. Reject duplicate emails only after row validation, retaining the first valid registration per normalized email. Rejected rows do not reserve an ID or email. Treat group_id as an opaque trimmed string, with empty meaning individual. Reject duplicate or missing required headers and unsupported extra headers explicitly rather than silently guessing. Return accepted participants in roster order, a CSV serialized with the six required headers in that order, and rejected row numbers and English reasons. CSV row numbers count the header as row 1. Structural errors return an English errors array with no participants or cleaned CSV.",
